<p class="eyebrow">About</p>

<h1>Stories, visuals, and observations.</h1>

<p>
  I'm Dipendra Pradhan.
</p>

<p>
  I spend a good amount of time looking at things—clouds moving across a hillside,
  rain collecting on electric wires, birds returning to the same roof every evening.
</p>

<p>
  I enjoy making images, but I'm equally drawn to words. Many of the stories and
  notes here began as <em>Hawrey Ko Katha</em>, a small corner of the internet where
  I wrote about places, people, weather, memory, and whatever happened to stay with me.
</p>

<p>
  One of my favourite films is <em>Into the Wild</em>. I often return to a line from it:
</p>

<blockquote>
  Happiness only real when shared.
</blockquote>

<p>
  I listen to Ray LaMontagne on quiet mornings and rainy afternoons.
</p>

<p>
  This website is a home for visuals, stories, observations, and things I don't
  want to forget.
</p>

